led on  a purchase price of $24,000 and both  walked away happy with the transaction  15:54 Spanish shipwreck gold bar when  one man was cleaning out the belongings  of his grandfather he found a gold bar  hidden away in a box its meltdown value  alone was $24,000 but what an expert  confirmed it was from a 1554 Spanish  ship record the price doubled instantly  through telling me that's worth $48,000  in that neighborhood  yeah 2001 Patriots Super Bowl ring  Patriots defensive back brought Williams  had a hard passion he decided to pawn  his 2001 Patriots Super Bowl ring for a  modest $2,600 he never came back for it  and the rain became the property of the  shop while similar rings have sold for  around thirty thousand dollars on  auction websites Rick isn't ready to let  go of his favorite item anytime soon  which is why he set the sale price on  this beauty to a whopping $100,000 John  F Kennedy cigar box the biggest payout  ever on Pawn Stars is thanks to a piece  of presidential history a seller walked  into the shop with a box of cigars that  once sat on john f kennedy's desk in the  Oval Office  after some haggling Rick managed to  purchase JFK a cigar box for $60,000 for  comparison a similar JFK humidor was  purchased by the publisher of cigar  aficionado in 1996 for five hundred and  seventy-five thousand dollars thanks for  watching subscribe to our YouTube  channel to watch more videos at the one  you just saw and leave us a comment to  let us know what you think of these pawn  star deals  [Music]
 

